  "description": "Alibaba-NLP gte-modernbert-base is a public Apache-2.0 English text embedding model for semantic search, RAG retrieval, long-document retrieval, and code retrieval. The active Forge TEI CUDA 1.9.3 profile supports B200, H200, L40S, and RTX6000, but repeated B300/SM103 diagnostics exited before readiness with `cuda compute cap 103 is not supported`. This separate active non-default CUDA 13 vLLM profile uses the already mirrored official vLLM 0.22.0 image digest sha256:0fec7ec5f3e6bc168e54899935fb0557da908a4832a1dbc88e2debcf2f889416, launches it with `--runner pooling`, and selects CLS pooling with activation enabled to match the upstream sentence-transformers pooling configuration. The 2026-06-03T04Z supervisor cycle moved the route off vLLM 0.21.0 because GHSA-94f4-hr76-p5j6 / CVE-2026-48746 is patched in vLLM 0.22.0, live-upserted the patched manifest, and ran a no-persist B300/uk-south1 smoke: 86.511 s startup, 76 ms client-wall request, 315.79 tokens/s, 1.27 GB VRAM, HTTP 200. Hugging Face metadata refreshed on 2026-05-31T14Z reports private=false, gated=false, disabled=false, pipeline_tag=sentence-similarity, library_name=transformers, license=apache-2.0, revision e7f32e3c00f91d699e8c43b53106206bcc72bb22, and a ModernBertModel config with no remote-code auto_map. The historical 2026-05-30T09Z vLLM 0.21.0 B300/uk-south1 hostPath probe passed with 3 warmups and 10 measured /v1/embeddings requests: 357.353 s startup, 72 ms client-wall p50, 333.33 tokens/s, and 1.27 GB VRAM. The historical 2026-05-31T14Z vLLM 0.21.0 non-B300 matrix added B200/us-central1 at 57.436 s startup and 163 ms p50, H200/eu-north2 at 71.201 s startup and 106 ms p50, and L40S/eu-north1 at 604.480 s startup including a 7m06s image pull and 108 ms p50. The 2026-05-30 cycle2 parity pass compared the vLLM B300 row against the TEI L40S reference over 10 synthetic general retrieval/control texts: min cosine 0.9999978567, max unit-vector delta 0.0009111334, max norm delta 0.0000000864, and 768 dimensions for every row. Keep default_eligible=false and is_latest=false because TEI remains the lighter latest route and RTX6000 has not been probed for this vLLM profile.",
